1,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":865585000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NjU1ODUwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:xr","name":"topic:xr","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-08-17T22:44:45Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T16:22:56Z","closed_at":"2026-09-16T16:22:29Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122512","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122512","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122512.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122512.patch","merged_at":"2026-09-16T16:22:29Z"},"body":"This PR makes it so that changes in the recommended size for the main OpenXR swapchain will only recreate the swapchain if it needs to get bigger. If the new recommended size is smaller, it just renders to a smaller part of the original swapchain.\r\n\r\nThis is mainly to better support the `XR_ANDROID_recommended_resolution` extension, which comes from the godot_openxr_vendors plugin, but these changes need to be in Godot itself, because it doesn't provide a new channel for the recommended resolution to come to Godot - it comes through `xrEnumerateViewConfigurationViews()` which is handled by Godot.\r\n\r\nThat said, this change does have a positive effect outside of just that extension. There's other reasons the main swapchain could get recreated, and this will make those more efficient too.\r\n\r\nThis led me to some interesting fixes:\r\n\r\n- We can't use the FDM from the OpenXR runtime if we are only rendering to part of the swapchain (otherwise the low resolution areas aren't \"centered\"), so this PR changes it to stop returning that one, and generate one instead. (We didn't notice it before, but this also affects the Meta dynamic resolution extension, and it's also fixed by the changes in this PR)\r\n- We were previously handling `foveation_level == 0` subtley wrong in `OpenXRFBFoveationExtension`: when the `XF_FB_foveation_extension` is enabled, we always make a foveation profile even if we set the the foveation level to `0`, however, we were only creating the swapchain with the right flags if `foveation_level > 0`, which technically means we can't set a foveation profile on the swapchain. This was leading to a crash on Samsung Galaxy XR without the changes here (but the change is correct in any case)\r\n\r\nSo, this PR also fixes those pre-existing issues - I could move them to their own PR, but at least the first one would look very different without the other changes here, so I opted to keep them together.\r\n\r\nThe one thing I'm unsure about, is if we should have a way to disable this behavior? If a developer artificially increases the resolution (by modifying `render_target_size_multiplier`) and then later resets it, they probably don't want the swapchain size to be preserved. Do we want to account for that?","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122512/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122512/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}